<title>ISRAEL: Elron 1996 EPS $0.56 vs $0.51.</title>
<headline>Elron 1996 EPS $0.56 vs $0.51.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Elron Electronic Industries.</p>
<p>			     (in thousands of dollars except EPS)</p>
<p>			  Q4 96	Q4 95	12-MTH 96  12-MTH 95</p>
<p>Income		  4,781	n/a	  14,859     15,719</p>
<p>Net Profit	    3,804	n/a	  11,279     10,304</p>
<p>Earnings per share   0.19	n/a	    0.56	 0.51</p>
<p>Elron, an electronics holding company, said group revenues were unchanged in 1996 at $1.2 billion compared with 1995.</p>
<p>It said attributable earnings from affiliated companies fell in the year to about $2.8 million from about $4.7 million in 1995, which it attributed to losses at the younger companies of the group.</p>
<p>For the fourth quarter, there was a rise in attributable earnings to $0.8 million from $0.5 million a year earlier, according to a statement by the company.</p>
<p>Elron did not provide full fourth-quarter 1995 results.</p>
<p>Elron's other income category was boosted in the final quarter to $3.8 million from $0.2 million a year earlier by the sale of 650,000 shares in Orbotech Ltd.</p>
<p>- Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502</p>
</text>
